"Davrar granted the gods their might, and they learned its structure and rebelled."
"Worship on Davrar is itself a mechanic in the Questors' game."
"The gods were mortals, since they could die."
"Khachi holds a jagged shard of divinity in place of a mana pool."
"Khachi says faith turns conviction into power, and the gods are not needed."
"Khachi's tenets are Humility, Virtue and Resolve; his Faith is in himself."
"Any crack in Khachi's righteousness weakens his power."
"Khachi's divine magic is weaker at night."
"Khachi's light: gold heals and heartens, yellow burns, white blinds and stuns."
"Khachi's blessings let him and others go without sleep, glowing as they meditate."
"Khachi's healing prayer ties wounds to glorious combat and washes them in golden light."
"Later, Khachi resurrects Stella by prayer, which drains his Faith and grows his shard."
"Later, Khachi's divinity grows new shards after great prayers, and once roughly doubles."
"Later, Khachi absorbs part of the god Deiman's remnant and his divinity grows tenfold or more."
"The remnant tested Khachi with the words SPEAK, WHY, HOW, UNDERSTAND and SUCCEED."
"Deiman was the god of righteous battle, a guardian turned tyrant, brought low by pride."
"Later, Khachi claims what is left of Deiman's godhead and the domain of Righteous Battle."
"Later, Khachi can raise the dead, a rare power Questors would want to control."
"Later, Khachi can kill by divine word and blind an area in judgement."
"Later, Khachi casts a three-part oath blessing: By Oath, By Deed, By Death."
"Dishonorable conduct by allies in an agreed duel voids Khachi's blessing."
"Later, divine light partly purifies blighted ground."
"Later, students gain faith-power by embracing Khachi's principles."
"Years later, Khachi's prayer 'Let speed find our steps' hastens travel."
